Fix: locking a dynamic vertex buffer with HBL_DISCARD makes the CPU wait for the GPU in every frame.

Description
  GL3PlusHardwareBuffer::lockImpl orphans the buffer with glBufferData(NULL) for HBL_DISCARD and then maps it with a
  synchronised glMapBufferRange. The orphaned storage is brand new and no queued GPU command can read it, so the
  synchronisation has nothing to protect, but the driver of the Intel Arc iGPU still waits for the GPU before it
  returns the pointer (call stack: BillboardSet::beginBillboards -> HardwareBuffer::lock -> driver wait
  NtGdiDdDDIWaitForSynchronizationObjectFromCpu, 17 % of the menu frame while the GPU 3D engine is 16 to 18 % busy).
  Every particle system with billboards, every overlay and every manual object locks a dynamic buffer like this
  once per frame.

  The fix maps the orphaned storage with GL_MAP_UNSYNCHRONIZED_BIT. This is the usual orphan and map pattern. The
  data that reaches the GPU, the buffer contents and the draw calls stay the same, so nothing looks different. It
  is the only change; HBL_NORMAL, HBL_READ_ONLY and HBL_NO_OVERWRITE keep their flags.

Affected OGRE file
  RenderSystems/GL3Plus/src/OgreGL3PlusHardwareBuffer.cpp, GL3PlusHardwareBuffer::lockImpl, the block
  "if(options == HBL_DISCARD)" (around line 78 of the OGRE 14 tree used here).

Reproduction
  Run a scene with several billboard particle systems on a driver that waits on the map (Intel Arc iGPU, GL 3+) and
  sample the main thread: the time spent in HardwareBuffer::lock is the wait. With the patch the wait is gone.

diff --git a/RenderSystems/GL3Plus/src/OgreGL3PlusHardwareBuffer.cpp b/RenderSystems/GL3Plus/src/OgreGL3PlusHardwareBuffer.cpp
--- a/RenderSystems/GL3Plus/src/OgreGL3PlusHardwareBuffer.cpp
+++ b/RenderSystems/GL3Plus/src/OgreGL3PlusHardwareBuffer.cpp
@@ -76,10 +76,15 @@ namespace Ogre {
         if (writeOnly)
         {
             if(options == HBL_DISCARD)
-                OGRE_CHECK_GL_ERROR(glBufferData(mTarget, mSizeInBytes, NULL, getGLUsage(mUsage)));
- 
-            access |= GL_MAP_WRITE_BIT;
+            {
+                OGRE_CHECK_GL_ERROR(glBufferData(mTarget, mSizeInBytes, NULL, getGLUsage(mUsage)));
+                // The storage was just orphaned: no queued command reads it, so no wait is needed
+                access |= GL_MAP_UNSYNCHRONIZED_BIT;
+            }
+
+            access |= GL_MAP_WRITE_BIT;
             if(options == HBL_NO_OVERWRITE)
                 access |= GL_MAP_UNSYNCHRONIZED_BIT;
         }
